    {
      "id": "09-cons",
      "index": 8,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "cons",
      "text": "Whole seeds can pass through partly undigested. Human research found much better lignan availability after crushing or milling, so grinding matters if you want more than the fibre. A sudden fibre jump can upset digestion. Large amounts can bring bloating, fullness, or diarrhoea. Build up gradually. Normal servings are much smaller than 100 grams. A spoonful is useful, but it delivers only a fraction of this stat sheet in a real meal.",
      "textSha256": "d06877c82d0a919975665e505dee974a7a974cf1ba5b558ea3f727763335da4d",
      "characterCount": 437,
